WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:02.168
-Well,

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.869
it looks like President Trump

00:00:03.869 --> 00:00:05.571
is trying his hardest
to get impeached again,

00:00:05.571 --> 00:00:07.006
and prosecuted,

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:09.174
after he called up
the Georgia secretary of state

00:00:09.174 --> 00:00:11.878
and pressured him to illegally
overturn election results

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:13.546
and lots of Republicans
are fully onboard.

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:15.515
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:19.652
♪♪

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:22.755
Well, it's 2021 and,
as predicted by the pundits,

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:24.857
things have finally
calmed down

00:00:24.857 --> 00:00:27.059
and the only question
left facing America is,

00:00:27.059 --> 00:00:28.995
"What are the late night hosts
going to talk about,

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:31.130
now that Donald Trump --"
What's that?

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.231
Who did he call?

00:00:32.231 --> 00:00:33.833
The Georgia secretary of state?
What for?

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:35.268
Begging for votes?!

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:36.335
But says who?

00:00:36.335 --> 00:00:37.871
It was recorded?!

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:39.105
But how could someone
record a call?

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:41.273
Oh, right, because it's 2021

00:00:41.273 --> 00:00:42.775
and anyone can record
a phone call

00:00:42.775 --> 00:00:44.844
and, if you're a notorious liar
who misrepresents phone calls

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:45.912
all the time,
you should probably assume

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:47.413
you're being recorded
from here on out?

00:00:47.413 --> 00:00:49.482
Yeah, but how long a phone call?
An hour?!

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:51.684
But, still, that means Trump
talked for, what, 30 minutes?

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:53.152
59 minutes?!

00:00:53.152 --> 00:00:55.355
Okay, but so what?
It's Trump being Trump, right?

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:56.789
-A dozen Republican senators

00:00:56.789 --> 00:00:59.358
and at least 140
House Republicans plan

00:00:59.358 --> 00:01:02.762 line:0%
to dispute next week's
Electoral College certification.

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:04.864 line:0%
The president's attorney
Rudy Giuliani

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:06.999 line:0%
called the Department
of Homeland Security

00:01:06.999 --> 00:01:08.268 line:0%
to see if it was possible

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:10.303 line:0%
for them to seize
voting machines.

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:11.571 line:0%
-If there's
evidence of fraud

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:13.673 line:0%
and it's substantial
and significant enough

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:16.308 line:0%
to affect the results
in a particular state,

00:01:16.308 --> 00:01:19.178 line:0%
then those election results
would have to be set aside.

00:01:19.178 --> 00:01:20.879 line:0%
-January 20th
cannot be changed.

00:01:20.879 --> 00:01:22.081 line:0%
That's constitutional.

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:23.816 line:0%
But this whole
certification thing,

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:25.952 line:0%
the days can be changed.
-Well, it can be changed,
actually.

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.987 line:0%
-Peter Navarro.
-We can go past that date.

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:29.522 line:0%
We can go past
that date.

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.023 line:0%
-Some of the
president's allies,

00:01:31.023 --> 00:01:33.492 line:0%
including his former National
Security Advisor Michael Flynn,

00:01:33.492 --> 00:01:37.563 line:0%
have suggested declaring martial
law to force new elections.

00:01:37.563 --> 00:01:38.798 line:0%
-Bombshell recording

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:40.900 line:0%
of a phone call
revealing President Trump

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.369 line:0%
pressuring an election
official in Georgia

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:45.538 line:0%
to overturn his defeat
to Joe Biden.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:56.015
-This is something far worse

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:57.650
than occurred in Watergate.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.353
-Damn it, I really thought this
year was going to be different.

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:02.021
I'd already started writing
down jokes

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:03.556
about budget reconciliation

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:07.427
and how Joe Biden's
secretary of state looks like,

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:11.831
I don't know,
a guy waiting in line

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:13.900
at the store?

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.734
Hope they had the mints
you liked, buddy!

00:02:15.734 --> 00:02:17.103
What -- I don't know,

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:19.372
The point is virtually the
entirety of the Republican Party

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:21.340
has started off the year
by making it clear --

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:22.742
in case it wasn't
clear before --

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:24.977
that they're actively trying
to destroy democracy.

00:02:24.977 --> 00:02:27.680
Also, this story was
yet another reminder that,

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:31.150
while we do a big countdown
and watch a ball drop,

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:33.486
the beginning of new years tend

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:35.855
to be a lot like the year
that just ended.

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:38.458
It's like the break between
rounds in a boxing match.

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:41.026
Sure, we got to sit on a stool
for a few minutes and sip water,

00:02:41.026 --> 00:02:43.162
but now it's right back
to concussion central

00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:45.431
and, predictably,
2021 is picking up

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:46.865
right where 2020 left off,

00:02:46.865 --> 00:02:48.167
with Trump
and the Republican Party

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:50.669
callously refusing
to do anything

00:02:50.669 --> 00:02:54.073
about the raging pandemic
that's killed 350,000 Americans,

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:56.309
or the botched vaccine rollout,

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:59.278
choosing, instead, to focus
on their unhinged attempts

00:02:59.278 --> 00:03:00.846
to light our democracy on fire.

00:03:00.846 --> 00:03:02.248
And we have to be clear-eyed
about this.

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:04.283
It's not just Trump.
They're all in on it,

00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:06.552
even if they're
conspicuously silent.

00:03:06.552 --> 00:03:08.187
They got their judges
and their tax cuts

00:03:08.187 --> 00:03:09.755
and this is the price
they were willing to pay.

00:03:09.755 --> 00:03:11.857
You don't get to take part
in a bank heist,

00:03:11.857 --> 00:03:13.593
then issue a statement
afterward that says...

00:03:20.432 --> 00:03:22.001
Now, we're going to go
through the entire phone call

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:23.536
in a minute because it's,
you know,

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:25.171
like insane and likely criminal,

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:26.806
but, first, it's important
to be straightforward

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:29.342
about what we're witnessing here
from the Republican Party.

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:31.944
This isn't just a matter
of political ambition

00:03:31.944 --> 00:03:34.447
eclipsing the shared commitment
to Democratic principles,

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:37.483
although there's certainly that
at play here, too.

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:40.219
It's not that Republicans
like Josh Hawley or Ted Cruz

00:03:40.219 --> 00:03:42.488
don't care about the
consequences of their actions.

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:44.824
They do. They want
to dismantle democracy.

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:46.960
It's an active goal
of the Republican Party
and has been for years,.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.728
The same party
that spent decades trying

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:49.829
to stop people from voting,

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:52.031
through voter ID laws
and poll closures

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:53.832
and requiring felons
to pay court fines

00:03:53.832 --> 00:03:55.501
and trying to toss out
legal mail ballots

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.936
is now trying to erase
the votes of their opponents,

00:03:57.936 --> 00:04:00.606
not because they think
their votes are illegitimate,

00:04:00.606 --> 00:04:03.575
but because they think their
opponents are illegitimate.

00:04:03.575 --> 00:04:04.877
We need to be clear about that.

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:07.213
If your coworker at Chipotle
spends years asking

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:09.949
if he can wrap you in a tortilla
and cover you in salsa

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:11.116
and sprinkle cheese
on your head,

00:04:11.116 --> 00:04:12.151
you can't be surprised

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:13.586
if you turn on the news one day

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:15.020
and see him arrested
for eating a guy.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:18.991
"Not Cannibal Gary!"

00:04:18.991 --> 00:04:20.192
And the Republicans who voted

00:04:20.192 --> 00:04:22.195
to acquit Trump
when he was impeached

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:24.564
for basically the same thing
are complicit, too.

00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:26.932
Remember when Maine Senator
Susan Collins voted

00:04:26.932 --> 00:04:29.869
to let Trump off the hook
for trying to extort Ukraine

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:32.304
to help him cheat in the
election, then said this?

00:04:32.304 --> 00:04:34.207
-I believe that the president

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:37.109
has learned from this case.

00:04:37.109 --> 00:04:39.345 line:0%
-What do you believe
the president has learned?

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:42.015 line:0%
-The president
has been impeached.

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:44.483 line:0%
That's a pretty big lesson.

00:04:44.483 --> 00:04:46.952
-That should go down
as the fourth-worst prediction
in history,

00:04:46.952 --> 00:04:49.155
after "People are going to love
this 'Cats' movie,"

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:50.689
"I think the Zune
is going to take off,"

00:04:50.689 --> 00:04:53.058
and "The gift of the season
is this 'Cats'-themed Zune."

00:04:53.058 --> 00:04:56.429 line:0%
Of course, that prediction was
absurd on its face at the time,

00:04:56.429 --> 00:04:58.130 line:0%
but it's especially pathetic
in hindsight.

00:04:58.130 --> 00:04:59.498
Trump is incapable
of learning lessons

00:04:59.498 --> 00:05:01.333
because he doesn't inhabit
our shared reality.

00:05:01.333 --> 00:05:02.335
That's clear on the tape.

00:05:02.335 --> 00:05:03.702
Trump thinks he's Al Pacino

00:05:03.702 --> 00:05:04.737
in "Glengarry Glen Ross,"

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:06.138
but, listening to the audio

00:05:06.138 --> 00:05:08.508
of his phone call,
it's clear he's Jack Lemmon

00:05:08.508 --> 00:05:10.543
in a phone booth,
begging for the good leads.

00:05:10.543 --> 00:05:12.745
You have to listen to the
entire, hour-long thing.

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:14.180
I mean, you don't have to.
It's pretty awful.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.148
But you could, if you had
like an hour to kill.

00:05:16.148 --> 00:05:17.583
The president
of the United States

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:18.918
sounded like
an inveterate gambler,

00:05:18.918 --> 00:05:21.620
begging his bookie
to float him for one more race.

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:23.289
[ As Trump ]
I just need 11,000 bucks.

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:25.057
I got a great horse.
He's a sure thing.

00:05:25.057 --> 00:05:27.560
His name is the Cataract Comet.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:28.961
And there's one moment,
in particular,

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:31.797
that really stayed with me,
that I can't get out of my head.

00:05:31.797 --> 00:05:32.832
When the president --

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:34.600
excuse me,
the president un-elect --

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.769
was speaking with the Georgia
secretary of state's

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:39.772
general counsel,
whose name is Ryan Germany,

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:42.375
and then, the president said
this very bizarre thing --

00:05:49.314 --> 00:05:50.950
I feel as though
I have a good read

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:53.085
on what the president
is doing, most of the time,

00:05:53.085 --> 00:05:54.687
because it's safe to bet

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:56.456
on the most morally corrupt
of the options,

00:05:56.456 --> 00:05:58.691
yet I truly don't know
what he was doing

00:05:58.691 --> 00:06:01.426
when he told this man,
"You have a nice last name."

00:06:01.426 --> 00:06:04.296
Was he snidely implying
that this lawyer was un-American

00:06:04.296 --> 00:06:05.631
because his last name
was Germany?

00:06:05.631 --> 00:06:08.367
Was he threatening
his last name, Mafia-style?

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:09.435
[ As Trump ]
Nice last name.

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:10.736
Would be a shame

00:06:10.736 --> 00:06:12.404
if anything happened to it.

00:06:12.404 --> 00:06:14.173
You'd just be Ryan.

00:06:14.173 --> 00:06:17.276
Going to be tough to get mail
with no last name, Ryan.

00:06:17.276 --> 00:06:18.810
Was it white supremacist
flirting?

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:20.479
[ As Trump ]
Germany?
That's a lovely name.

00:06:20.479 --> 00:06:23.382
I like that name.
Uber alles.

00:06:23.382 --> 00:06:25.684
Or was it an actual attempt
to complement,

00:06:25.684 --> 00:06:28.988
in an effort to sweet talk him,
in hopes that the lawyer

00:06:28.988 --> 00:06:30.656
for the Georgia Secretary
of State's Office

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:34.393
would say, [ Southern accent ]
"Well, my goodness, Mr. Trump!

00:06:34.393 --> 00:06:37.429
You have set my heart aflutter
with your silver tongue.

00:06:37.429 --> 00:06:40.700
Now, exactly how many votes did
you say you would be needing?

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:43.402
Trump's combination
of drowsiness and frantic energy

00:06:43.402 --> 00:06:45.604
are on display in full force
throughout the call.

00:06:45.604 --> 00:06:48.073
It's like he just had a meal
of turkey stuffed with Red Bull.

00:06:48.073 --> 00:06:49.575
At one point,
Trump told Raffensperger

00:06:49.575 --> 00:06:51.476
that he was damaging
the Republican Party

00:06:51.476 --> 00:06:53.012
for the upcoming
runoff election.

00:06:59.551 --> 00:07:01.954
Vote negative? Well,
at least Trump's subconscious

00:07:01.954 --> 00:07:03.289
is paying attention to COVID.

00:07:05.958 --> 00:07:07.893
It's tempting to think
Trump is unique

00:07:07.893 --> 00:07:11.564
because he's an unhinged buffoon
who cajoles and threatens

00:07:11.564 --> 00:07:13.365
and admits his criminality
out loud.

00:07:13.365 --> 00:07:15.234
Meanwhile, his minions,
guys like Josh Hawley

00:07:15.234 --> 00:07:16.669
and Ted Cruz and Ron Johnson,

00:07:16.669 --> 00:07:20.105 line:0%
cosplay as noble statesmen
and use lofty rhetoric

00:07:20.105 --> 00:07:21.774 line:0%
to achieve the same
corrupt goals.

00:07:21.774 --> 00:07:23.643 line:0%
-We've seen,
in the last two months,

00:07:23.643 --> 00:07:26.846 line:0%
unprecedented allegations
of voter fraud

00:07:26.846 --> 00:07:30.216 line:0%
and that's produced a deep,
deep distrust

00:07:30.216 --> 00:07:33.018 line:0%
of our democratic process
across the country.

00:07:33.018 --> 00:07:34.987 line:0%
I think we in Congress
have an obligation

00:07:34.987 --> 00:07:36.021 line:0%
to do something about that.

00:07:36.021 --> 00:07:37.723 line:0%
We have an obligation
to protect

00:07:37.723 --> 00:07:40.025 line:0%
the integrity
of the democratic system.

00:07:40.025 --> 00:07:42.929
-We are not acting to thwart
the democratic process.

00:07:42.929 --> 00:07:45.330
We're acting to protect it.

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:47.232
The fact of the matter is
that we have

00:07:47.232 --> 00:07:49.668
a unsustainable state of affairs
in this country

00:07:49.668 --> 00:07:51.804
where we have tens
of millions of people

00:07:51.804 --> 00:07:54.907
that do not view these
election results as legitimate.

00:07:54.907 --> 00:07:56.174
-Now, when Republicans,

00:07:56.174 --> 00:07:58.144
74 million Americans,

00:07:58.144 --> 00:08:00.212 line:0%
have concerns
about election integrity,

00:08:00.212 --> 00:08:02.047 line:0%
we're supposed to just
sit down and shut up?

00:08:02.047 --> 00:08:04.016 line:0%
I mean, somebody has
to stand up here.

00:08:04.016 --> 00:08:08.621 line:0%
You've got 74 million Americans
who feel disenfranchised,

00:08:08.621 --> 00:08:10.689 line:0%
who feel like their vote
doesn't matter.

00:08:10.689 --> 00:08:12.892
-Ted Cruz definitely
would've been the lawyer

00:08:12.892 --> 00:08:14.760
representing the city
in Salem v. Witches.

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:17.362
[ As Cruz ]
We keep hearing
there's no evidence

00:08:17.362 --> 00:08:19.331
that these girls are witches,
but I say,

00:08:19.331 --> 00:08:22.401
why not throw them in the river,
so we can know for sure?

00:08:22.401 --> 00:08:24.303
Republicans think
the election was rigged

00:08:24.303 --> 00:08:27.973
because you guys keep
telling them it was rigged.

00:08:27.973 --> 00:08:30.342
These guys would yell, "Echo,"
into a canyon

00:08:30.342 --> 00:08:32.311
and then tell you that someone
across the canyon

00:08:32.311 --> 00:08:33.512
is yelling, "Echo."

00:08:33.512 --> 00:08:35.414
And, now,
you want an investigation

00:08:35.414 --> 00:08:36.749
into whether
the election was rigged

00:08:36.749 --> 00:08:38.250
because people believed you
when you lied

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:39.317
and said the election
was rigged?

00:08:39.317 --> 00:08:40.519
Also, haven't we
done this already?

00:08:40.519 --> 00:08:41.987
I mean, what was that weird

00:08:41.987 --> 00:08:44.756
adult puppet show with Rudy
and Chardonnay Charlotte?

00:08:44.756 --> 00:08:47.292
You want us to hear more
about this nonsense?

00:08:47.292 --> 00:08:50.395
Look, the local weirdo can take
five minutes at a town meeting

00:08:50.395 --> 00:08:51.697
to talk about how
he saw Bigfoot,

00:08:51.697 --> 00:08:53.465
but, at some point,
he has to yield the floor,

00:08:53.465 --> 00:08:55.600
so we can discuss potholes
or, I don't know,

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:56.969
the [bleep] pandemic.

00:08:56.969 --> 00:08:58.804
Also, stop with this [bleep]

00:08:58.804 --> 00:09:01.439
about the 74 million Americans
who feel disenfranchised.

00:09:01.439 --> 00:09:03.842
What about the 81 million
Americans who voted for Biden,

00:09:03.842 --> 00:09:05.711
who you're currently trying
to disenfranchise?

00:09:05.711 --> 00:09:08.213
Maybe we need a committee
to look into their concerns.

00:09:08.213 --> 00:09:09.515
Hey, we could even
call witnesses.

00:09:09.515 --> 00:09:11.584
Maybe the Georgia secretary
of state or his lawyer

00:09:11.584 --> 00:09:14.620
could testify before Cruz's
dumbass electoral commission.

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:16.855
[ As Cruz ]
The committee now calls
to the stand Ryan --

00:09:16.855 --> 00:09:20.259
and I will ask the court
to maintain their composure --

00:09:20.259 --> 00:09:21.727
Germany.
-[ Murmuring ] Germany.

00:09:21.727 --> 00:09:23.228
That's a nice name.
That's a very nice name.

00:09:23.228 --> 00:09:25.664
I don't think I've ever heard
a name that sounds so terrific.

00:09:25.664 --> 00:09:28.067
I hope somebody
complements his name.

00:09:28.067 --> 00:09:29.802
[ Laughter ]

00:09:29.802 --> 00:09:31.337
These guys tried to use
lofty rhetoric

00:09:31.337 --> 00:09:32.771
to conceal
what they were really doing,

00:09:32.771 --> 00:09:34.806
which was the exact same thing
Trump was trying to do --

00:09:34.806 --> 00:09:37.009
steal an election
and overthrow democracy.

00:09:37.009 --> 00:09:38.710
But, with this call
to Raffensperger,

00:09:38.710 --> 00:09:40.245
Trump ripped off the mask

00:09:40.245 --> 00:09:41.947
and revealed
what was really going on.

00:09:41.947 --> 00:09:45.851
He made it crystal-clear exactly
what those 140 GOP House members

00:09:45.851 --> 00:09:48.086
and a dozen senators
will be supporting on Wednesday.

00:09:48.086 --> 00:09:50.222
They're not standing up
for election integrity

00:09:50.222 --> 00:09:52.491
or trying to restore faith
in our democracy.

00:09:52.491 --> 00:09:55.094
They're petty henchmen
in a harebrained scheme

00:09:55.094 --> 00:09:58.430
to steal an election, hatched
by a deranged wannabe tyrant

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:00.533
who talks like a Mafia boss
with a head injury.

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:37.036
There's a real "Office" vibe
when you hear him saying --

00:10:37.036 --> 00:10:38.671
[ As Trump ]
You can't do that to Ryan.

00:10:38.671 --> 00:10:39.905
[ Laughter ]

00:10:39.905 --> 00:10:43.209
Not sweet Ryan!

00:10:43.209 --> 00:10:44.343
But, seriously, it is about time

00:10:44.343 --> 00:10:46.077
someone gives this poor man
a break.

00:10:46.077 --> 00:10:47.746
After everything
he's accomplished.

00:10:47.746 --> 00:10:49.047
What have you done?

00:10:49.047 --> 00:10:51.150
He got into UPenn,
despite someone else jumping in

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:52.918
and taking his SATs for him.

00:10:52.918 --> 00:10:54.553
Didn't get to fight
for his country in Vietnam

00:10:54.553 --> 00:10:57.323
because either his right
or left foot had bone spurs.

00:10:57.323 --> 00:10:59.357
It's private!
You can't ask him!

00:10:59.357 --> 00:11:01.360
Managed to succeed in business
with nothing but his grit

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:02.894
and a million-dollar loan
from his father.

00:11:02.894 --> 00:11:04.229
The list goes on and on.

00:11:04.229 --> 00:11:05.731
That's definitely
what you heard,

00:11:05.731 --> 00:11:09.668
is definitely the voice of a man
who's been in debt before.

00:11:09.668 --> 00:11:11.503
He sounds like he's begging
the waiter at a steakhouse

00:11:11.503 --> 00:11:12.904
to let him skate on the bill.

00:11:12.904 --> 00:11:14.640
[ As Trump ]
Gary, please.
You know I'm good for it.

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:17.609
My wallet's just a little light,
right after I bet it all

00:11:17.609 --> 00:11:19.111
on the Cataract Comet.

00:11:19.111 --> 00:11:21.213
[ Laughter ]
Bumped right into the wall.

00:11:21.213 --> 00:11:25.384
[ Fresh laughter ]
You'd think he'd remember
to turn left.

00:11:25.384 --> 00:11:27.686
I thought it was
an ironic nickname,

00:11:27.686 --> 00:11:29.121
like Cannibal Gary.

00:11:29.121 --> 00:11:30.322
He ate a guy?

00:11:30.322 --> 00:11:33.825
[ Laughter ]

00:11:33.825 --> 00:11:36.996
And, aside from the begging
and threats and cajoling,

00:11:36.996 --> 00:11:38.530
there were also the times
when it was clear

00:11:38.530 --> 00:11:40.265
Trump was deeply immersed

00:11:40.265 --> 00:11:43.168
in the details of deranged
conspiracy theories

00:11:43.168 --> 00:11:45.270
that you can only find
on Facebook and Newsmax

00:11:45.270 --> 00:11:47.906
and in the darkest recesses
of the right-wing Internet.

00:11:47.906 --> 00:11:50.475
At one point,
he kept asking, nonsensically,

00:11:50.475 --> 00:11:52.111
whether voting machines
have been replaced,

00:11:52.111 --> 00:11:53.312
including what he called --

00:11:53.312 --> 00:11:55.814
and again, this is a very
common tech term,

00:11:55.814 --> 00:11:58.184
for people who know computers --
the inner parts.

00:12:40.893 --> 00:12:42.794
Shredded ballots,
moving machines,

00:12:42.794 --> 00:12:44.930
new machine parts --
just trying everything.

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:47.332
It's like a guy
without a silver bullet

00:12:47.332 --> 00:12:49.801
brainstorming other ways
to kill a werewolf.

00:12:49.801 --> 00:12:51.636
[ As Trump ]
What about, uh,

00:12:51.636 --> 00:12:53.272
two regular bullets?

00:12:53.272 --> 00:12:55.874
Is that something
that might work?

00:12:55.874 --> 00:12:57.742
"There's no reason to think
that would work, sir."

00:12:57.742 --> 00:12:59.611
Now, so, I know

00:12:59.611 --> 00:13:02.414
Frankenstein hates fire.

00:13:02.414 --> 00:13:05.217
And, Frankenstein and Wolf Man
are dear friends.

00:13:05.217 --> 00:13:07.720
Do we think fire might work?

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:08.854
Ryan?

00:13:08.854 --> 00:13:09.854
[ Laughter ]

00:13:09.854 --> 00:13:11.022
"No, sir."

00:13:11.022 --> 00:13:13.726
Oh, uh, look, Ryan!

00:13:13.726 --> 00:13:17.096
Uh, I'm the last guy
who wants to bring this up,

00:13:17.096 --> 00:13:18.597
but do we think --

00:13:18.597 --> 00:13:21.700
do we think the werewolf
might die

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:24.336
if we gave it COVID?

00:13:24.336 --> 00:13:26.338
And then, at another point,
he repeated some deranged lie

00:13:26.338 --> 00:13:28.740
about military ballots.
It was so off-the-rails,

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:30.208
even his own aides and lawyers

00:13:30.208 --> 00:13:32.578
who were on the call
went dead silent.

00:14:11.050 --> 00:14:12.785
[ Laughter ]

00:14:12.785 --> 00:14:13.853
[ As Trump ]
You guy-- you guys,

00:14:13.853 --> 00:14:17.055
I-I think you might
all be on mute.

00:14:17.055 --> 00:14:18.590
Can we check?

00:14:18.590 --> 00:14:21.060
Can we check to make sure
Ryan's not on mute?

00:14:21.060 --> 00:14:23.829
[ Laughter ]

00:14:23.829 --> 00:14:25.331
You guys?

00:14:25.331 --> 00:14:26.965
[ Laughter ]

00:14:26.965 --> 00:14:28.767
That was like getting high

00:14:28.767 --> 00:14:30.769
and telling an embarrassing
story at a party.

00:14:30.769 --> 00:14:32.370
You know, like when someone
mentions karaoke

00:14:32.370 --> 00:14:35.406
and then you say, "Oh, yeah.
I know what you mean.

00:14:35.406 --> 00:14:38.177
One time, I got wasted

00:14:38.177 --> 00:14:40.545
and I try to sing
'Baby Got Back,'

00:14:40.545 --> 00:14:43.649
but then I vomited
and slipped on my own vomit

00:14:43.649 --> 00:14:46.352
and split my pants and farted.

00:14:46.352 --> 00:14:48.854
We've all been there, right?

00:14:48.854 --> 00:14:50.989
Right?

00:14:50.989 --> 00:14:54.125
In the vomit.

00:14:54.125 --> 00:14:55.994
Farting.

00:14:55.994 --> 00:14:59.297
Debbie, you have --
You haven't?"

00:14:59.297 --> 00:15:00.698
There were even times
when Trump himself

00:15:00.698 --> 00:15:02.934
couldn't keep his lies straight.
At one point, he seemed

00:15:02.934 --> 00:15:05.271
to exhaust himself
and just drop the pretense.

00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:37.603
I just like to imagine
what everyone else was doing

00:15:37.603 --> 00:15:38.871
on the other end
of the phone call

00:15:38.871 --> 00:15:41.206
while Trump was rambling
like a lunatic for an hour.

00:15:41.206 --> 00:15:43.108
It's like when you put
your grandpa on speakerphone

00:15:43.108 --> 00:15:44.409
while you do household chores
and then,

00:15:44.409 --> 00:15:46.912
he just casually confesses
to a crime in the middle.

00:15:46.912 --> 00:15:48.646
"So, anyways, the golf club
got mad at me

00:15:48.646 --> 00:15:51.149
for not fixing my divots,
so I complained to the manager

00:15:51.149 --> 00:15:53.218
and told him my arthritis
has been acting up

00:15:53.218 --> 00:15:54.719
and I can't find
my hernia donut,

00:15:54.719 --> 00:15:57.189
so I killed your grandmother
and the A.C. isn't working.

00:15:57.189 --> 00:15:58.624
Alright, talk to you later."

00:15:58.624 --> 00:16:00.659
Although, personally, I think
my favorite part of the call was

00:16:00.659 --> 00:16:02.727
when Trump repeated
yet another conspiracy theory,

00:16:02.727 --> 00:16:05.263
this time claiming that people
had moved out of the state

00:16:05.263 --> 00:16:06.631
and illegally voted in Georgia.

00:16:06.631 --> 00:16:09.301
When our friend Germany
explained that, actually,

00:16:09.301 --> 00:16:10.836
those people
had moved out years ago,

00:16:10.836 --> 00:16:12.904
then legitimately moved back
to Georgia

00:16:12.904 --> 00:16:13.973
and voted legally there,

00:16:13.973 --> 00:16:16.308
Trump dismissed
that idea as ridiculous.

00:16:53.712 --> 00:16:55.747
-[ Laughing ] There's
that silver tongue again.

00:16:55.747 --> 00:16:58.083
[ As Trump ]
You mean to tell me people
actually missed Georgia --

00:16:58.083 --> 00:17:00.852
Georgia -- so much,
they moved back voluntarily?

00:17:00.852 --> 00:17:02.654
That burning backwater [bleep]?

00:17:02.654 --> 00:17:04.923
I'd rather be dead
than move to Georgia.

00:17:04.923 --> 00:17:07.459
And then, if I was dead,
I'd vote for Biden.

00:17:07.459 --> 00:17:08.527
Ryan.

00:17:08.527 --> 00:17:09.861
[ Laughter ]

00:17:09.861 --> 00:17:11.063 line:0%
Ryan, have you looked --

00:17:11.063 --> 00:17:12.497 line:0%
have you checked
if dead people --

00:17:12.497 --> 00:17:15.300 line:0%
Ryan -- Ryan.

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:17.703 line:0%
Ryan, I'm just talking
to you now, Ryan.

00:17:17.703 --> 00:17:20.471 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
This isn't for Brad.

00:17:20.471 --> 00:17:24.576 line:0%
Ryan, I just need 11,700 votes.

00:17:24.576 --> 00:17:25.910 line:0%
Ryan.

00:17:25.910 --> 00:17:29.381 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
Ryan's on mute again.

00:17:29.381 --> 00:17:31.183
And it's important to note
that Trump was not

00:17:31.183 --> 00:17:32.884
the only White House official
on this call.

00:17:32.884 --> 00:17:34.186
His chief of staff,
Mark Meadows,

00:17:34.186 --> 00:17:35.821
tried, at one point,
to broker an agreement

00:17:35.821 --> 00:17:37.789
to let Trump's team look at data

00:17:37.789 --> 00:17:39.757
they were legally not allowed
to have access to,

00:17:39.757 --> 00:17:42.894
despite the fact that they've
lost about 60 court cases

00:17:42.894 --> 00:17:44.496
and that the votes
in Georgia were certified

00:17:44.496 --> 00:17:45.863
after being recounted
three times.

00:17:45.863 --> 00:17:48.667
And, at one point, Meadows
slyly tried to insinuate

00:17:48.667 --> 00:17:51.336
that everyone agreed
they should investigate

00:17:51.336 --> 00:17:53.205
the president's
conspiracy theories,

00:17:53.205 --> 00:17:54.606
before Germany shot him down.

00:18:40.651 --> 00:18:42.654
He's like a teacher who doesn't
want to talk to a parent

00:18:42.654 --> 00:18:44.589
about her son's
math grades anymore.

00:18:44.589 --> 00:18:46.692
"Look, I don't think
he's an "A" student

00:18:46.692 --> 00:18:48.126
who needs to recognize
his potential,

00:18:48.126 --> 00:18:49.460
but I'm happy to sit down
with you

00:18:49.460 --> 00:18:52.764
to show you exactly how [bleep]
he is at fractions."

00:18:52.764 --> 00:18:55.333
Meadows, Hawley, Cruz,
officials at the highest levels

00:18:55.333 --> 00:18:57.302
of the Republican Party,
are all complicit in this.

00:18:57.302 --> 00:18:58.536
And, as for Trump,

00:18:58.536 --> 00:19:00.671
what he did here very much
looks like a crime,

00:19:00.671 --> 00:19:03.174
for which he should be
both impeached and prosecuted.

00:19:03.174 --> 00:19:04.810
Raffensperger
even suggested today

00:19:04.810 --> 00:19:06.611
that the Fulton County
district attorney wanted

00:19:06.611 --> 00:19:07.712
to investigate it.

00:19:07.712 --> 00:19:09.515
There's a Georgia state law
against...

00:19:12.150 --> 00:19:13.251
...and there's a federal law

00:19:13.251 --> 00:19:15.053
that makes it a crime
when someone...

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:23.862
Look, I'm no lawyer,

00:19:23.862 --> 00:19:25.931
but that sounds exactly
like what Trump did.

00:19:25.931 --> 00:19:28.099
It's almost like they wrote
the law specifically

00:19:28.099 --> 00:19:29.301
with Trump in mind.

00:19:29.301 --> 00:19:30.401
"Should we add anything
about not being able

00:19:30.401 --> 00:19:31.636
to close an umbrella?

00:19:31.636 --> 00:19:34.472
Will that make it clear
who we're talking about?"

00:19:34.472 --> 00:19:36.307
Just because the GOP's attempt
to steal this election

00:19:36.307 --> 00:19:37.442
isn't going to work, this time,

00:19:37.442 --> 00:19:38.576
doesn't mean
it won't work in the future.

00:19:38.576 --> 00:19:40.311
Unless there are consequences,

00:19:40.311 --> 00:19:42.380
they're just going to keep going
until they succeed

00:19:42.380 --> 00:19:44.149
and Democrats need
to remember that

00:19:44.149 --> 00:19:45.283
and do something about it now.

00:19:45.283 --> 00:19:47.218
Even if Trump fades away --
which I doubt --

00:19:47.218 --> 00:19:48.253
he's not alone.

00:19:48.253 --> 00:19:49.921
The Republican Party,
as a whole,

00:19:49.921 --> 00:19:51.022
is a threat to democracy.

00:19:51.022 --> 00:19:52.223
That's the lesson, here,
and it's...

00:19:52.223 --> 00:19:54.292
-A pretty big lesson.

00:19:54.292 --> 00:19:55.994
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:19:55.994 --> 00:19:59.564
♪♪

